# vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/permit_tools.py

The executor-seam permission gate: any tool call whose name is outside a fixed permitted set is refused with an error tool message and never executed. Fails closed.

Source: `vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/permit_tools.py` (lines 1-80)
Executor: code
Called from: `options/graph_builder.py:436-437` when `permitted_tool_calls` is not null (always on the one-shot path; on streaming only when `StreamingOptions.permitted_tool_calls` is set); `options/subagents.py:140-141` per subagent under the same streaming condition

// src: vvaharness/backends/harness/deepagents/permit_tools.py:38-77
PermitTools(permitted) {
  wrap_tool_call(request, handler) {
    name = request.tool_call.name || ""
    require name in permitted => {
      log TOOL_CALL_REFUSED with the tool name only (never arguments)
      return ToolMessage("Error: tool '$name' is not permitted in this session and was not executed.", status="error", tool_call_id=request.tool_call.id)
    }
    return handler(request)
  }
}
